From 17fb293c2af063a672481e920c83502386aac3ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:13:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] driver core: Clean up old glue directory after device_move

A successful device_move() can leave an empty class glue directory
under the old parent. Remove it after the device has moved to prevent
a later device addition from reusing a glue directory whose sysfs
node was removed with its former parent.

On stm32mp1, stopping the NCM gadget and unbinding/rebinding DWC2
can make the next configfs start fail with -ENOENT while reparenting
usb0. The UDC core then reports no available UDC, even though DWC2
registered. Cleaning up the old glue directory prevents reusing the
sysfs node removed with the old gadget parent.

Error log seen when the issue happens:
dwc2 49000000.usb-otg: EPs: 9, dedicated fifos, 952 entries in SPRAM
dwc2 49000000.usb-otg: DWC OTG Controller
dwc2 49000000.usb-otg: new USB bus registered, assigned bus number 2
dwc2 49000000.usb-otg: irq 59, io mem 0x49000000
kobject: kobject_add_internal failed for usb0 (error: -2 parent: net)
udc 49000000.usb-otg: failed to start g1: -2
configfs-gadget.g1 gadget.0: probe with driver configfs-gadget.g1 failed
  with error -2
UDC core: g1: couldn't find an available UDC or it's busy

Fixes: ec35c1969650 ("usb: gadget: f_ncm: Fix net_device lifecycle with device_move")
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:GPT-6-Luna
Signed-off-by: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I35baefc20b8d9d71cf29ad5762d30392e6851ce4
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/617675
Tested-by: Jerome BESNARD <jerome.besnard@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Christian BRUEL <christian.bruel@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/base/core.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
index d577c7d7aacd..046cb3e41a3c 100644
--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -4670,6 +4670,7 @@ int device_move(struct device *dev, struct device *new_parent,
 	int error;
 	struct device *old_parent;
 	struct kobject *new_parent_kobj;
+	struct kobject *old_glue_dir;
 
 	dev = get_device(dev);
 	if (!dev)
@@ -4686,6 +4687,7 @@ int device_move(struct device *dev, struct device *new_parent,
 
 	pr_debug("device: '%s': %s: moving to '%s'\n", dev_name(dev),
 		 __func__, new_parent ? dev_name(new_parent) : "<NULL>");
+	old_glue_dir = get_glue_dir(dev);
 	error = kobject_move(&dev->kobj, new_parent_kobj);
 	if (error) {
 		cleanup_glue_dir(dev, new_parent_kobj);
@@ -4722,6 +4724,7 @@ int device_move(struct device *dev, struct device *new_parent,
 			goto out;
 		}
 	}
+	cleanup_glue_dir(dev, old_glue_dir);
 	switch (dpm_order) {
 	case DPM_ORDER_NONE:
 		break;
-- 
